windowResizeT -- windows stroke 3 (SEQ 750, 2026-11-22): resize and close. A delta of resizeLightT's preamble (copied, then
patched). Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh, run at GCSTRESS=1000. No window is shown.

The window is opened with a REQUEST (wrReq form:=firstLight), not a laid-out copy: it lays the form out itself through
utilities' windowLay, keeps the request, and is found afterwards by the form the request names (readWindow, windowClick,
windowResize and windowClose all take form:=firstLight).

open     firstLight as declared, 500x600; resizeLightT's four small points.
big      windowResize to 1200x600: the window takes the size and the view's own viewDidEndLiveResize runs, as when a drag
         ends. The frame goes to formFrames and setFrame lays out from there (windowLay): the page and the five points are
         resizeLightT's RG-2, compared by value in formsPop. The store's entry is read and cleared, as redrawWindow leaves it.
click    a point on ok at the big size: the window lays out again BY ITSELF after the click (stroke 2 left that to the
         fixture). The size is still 1200x600 and ok, selected, is defaultLook's lightBlue.
small    resized back to 500x600: resizeLightT's small points, ok still selected.
close    resized to 1200x600 again, then closed as the close button closes it: keepFrame alone, the frame kept in
         formFrames (entry 1). The window is forgotten: readWindow refuses by name.
reopen   the same request again, naming no frame: setFrame takes the kept frame, so the window opens 1200x600, and the
         entry is cleared.
errant   windowResize and windowClose for a form no window shows: refused by name.
definition  firstLight still declares 500x600.
